  {
    "@id": "https://www.centrekabir.com/temporary/5258afa6-0569-440c-b891-7f9bca93863d",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.centrekabir.com/en/events/songs-of-dharwad/var/ri-0.l-L2"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\n\n\t\t \n\t \n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\nCANCELLED due to evolving Covid-19 situation.\n\n\n\t\t \n\t \t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\nPandit Kaivalya Kumar, hailing from Dharwad in India, is an exciting young exponent of Kirana Gharana. His grandfather Ganapat Rao Gurav was a first-batch disciple of the venerable Abdul Karim Khan, the founder of Kirana Gharana. He brings a certain flamboyance to his renditions with sharp tonal quality, agile pace, vocal tenor and feverish dedication to music. He will be accompanied on tabla by the equally flamboyant Pandit Subhen Chatterjee and on melodious harmonium by Pandit Sanatan Goswami. This is a rare vocal concert of Hindustani music, both meditative and melodious, evocative of the good old days of the legendary Bhimsen Joshi and Amir Khan, simply not to be missed!\n\n\n\n\t\t \n\t \t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t \n\t \n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t \n\t \n"
      }
    ],
